0.2
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,200
Venus
Radonitsa Colony

1
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:46,912
(Coronal)
What is it that people desire?

2
00:00:48,038 --> 00:00:50,749
Within the ordinary lives
we lived until yesterday...

3
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:55,003
When suddenly, an unexpected door of fate
appears before us...

4
00:00:55,087 --> 00:00:57,756
(Impact sound)

5
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:02,970
(Explosion)

6
00:01:19,152 --> 00:01:21,738
(Wistario)
Why our town… why…!?

7
00:01:21,822 --> 00:01:23,073
(Girl crying)

8
00:01:23,156 --> 00:01:24,449
(Demnar)
This is...

9
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:27,035
It appears to be
a Mobile Suit attack…

10
00:01:27,119 --> 00:01:27,953
(Wistario)
A Mobile Suit!?

11
00:01:32,207 --> 00:01:33,834
(Demnar)
Young master! This way!

12
00:01:33,917 --> 00:01:34,960
(Wistario)
Right!

13
00:01:36,044 --> 00:01:39,047
(Demnar)
The basic controls are the same as
the one you usually use...

14
00:01:39,131 --> 00:01:40,924
the Hloekk Graze.

15
00:01:41,008 --> 00:01:44,219
However, the Ahab Reactor output
is more than double.

16
00:01:44,678 --> 00:01:48,557
We will support you from here as well,
but please be careful.

17
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:49,808
(Wistario)
Thanks.

18
00:01:50,309 --> 00:01:51,351
Hm?

19
00:01:52,019 --> 00:01:55,647
Gramps, what does “Hajiroboshi” mean?

20
00:01:55,731 --> 00:01:58,442
(Demnar)
That is this machine’s pet name.

21
00:02:02,571 --> 00:02:03,780
(Wistario)
I see.

22
00:02:03,864 --> 00:02:04,698
Then…

23
00:02:05,782 --> 00:02:08,285
Let’s go, Hajiroboshi.

24
00:02:13,916 --> 00:02:16,960
(Coronal)
When a light...

25
00:02:17,044 --> 00:02:22,257
capable of changing your life,
your future, everything...

26
00:02:22,883 --> 00:02:24,092
appears before you…

27
00:02:32,517 --> 00:02:37,397
I’ll never forgive you
for scarring my town!

28
00:02:41,234 --> 00:02:44,946
(Coronal)
My name is Coronal Xhosa.

29
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,949
Do you possess a Ring?

30
00:02:47,282 --> 00:02:48,116
A Ring?

31
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,242
Ah...

32
00:02:49,618 --> 00:02:51,119
You mean…

33
00:02:53,246 --> 00:02:54,289
this?

34
00:02:54,373 --> 00:02:55,415
(Coronal)
Heh…

35
00:02:57,542 --> 00:02:59,461
Graturatio.

36
00:02:59,544 --> 00:03:01,046
Congratulations.

37
00:03:03,548 --> 00:03:07,260
You have earned the right
to participate in the “Urdr-Hunt.”

38
00:03:14,142 --> 00:03:17,312
(Coronal)
Guide and navigator,
Coronal Xhosa.

39
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:21,066
One who opens doors
and leads others onward…

40
00:03:21,149 --> 00:03:22,067
However...

41
00:03:22,609 --> 00:03:27,197
looking back now, perhaps the door of fate
had opened before me as well...

42
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:30,075
just as equally…

43
00:03:30,951 --> 00:03:34,079
I doubt I will ever forget
that day.

44
00:03:34,955 --> 00:03:35,998
Yes.

45
00:03:36,415 --> 00:03:40,502
The day I met
Wistario Afam.

46
00:03:42,421 --> 00:03:44,423
{\an8}♪～

46.2
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Mobile Suit Gundam: Iron-Blooded Orphans
Urdr-Hunt – Path of the Little Challenger

47
00:03:55,267 --> 00:03:57,894
{\an8}♪ The signal that it had begun

48
00:03:57,978 --> 00:04:02,023
♪ I can’t remember it at all

49
00:04:02,107 --> 00:04:07,904
♪ Before I knew it,
I had already been running forever

50
00:04:07,988 --> 00:04:10,574
♪ So much it makes me want to cry

51
00:04:10,657 --> 00:04:15,829
♪ I realized people
are never truly equal

52
00:04:15,912 --> 00:04:20,041
♪ Reality is cruel

53
00:04:20,125 --> 00:04:26,757
♪ Beaten down,
aching with unbearable loneliness

54
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:32,763
♪ Even so,
my legs still keep moving

55
00:04:32,846 --> 00:04:37,017
♪ So no matter how far

56
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,644
♪ I’ll go even farther

57
00:04:39,728 --> 00:04:43,607
♪ Even if this should become

58
00:04:43,690 --> 00:04:45,567
♪ a night with no dawn

59
00:04:45,650 --> 00:04:49,905
♪ Even if the thing I wished for
that day

60
00:04:49,988 --> 00:04:52,407
♪ was more than I deserved

61
00:04:52,491 --> 00:04:58,789
♪ it moves me
beyond all control

62
00:04:58,872 --> 00:05:05,378
♪ It keeps pushing me onward,
again and again

63
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:12,302
{\an8}～♪

64
00:05:14,513 --> 00:05:16,932
(Coronal)
Urdr-Hunt Memorandum.

65
00:05:17,307 --> 00:05:20,727
Today, by order
of my master “N”...

66
00:05:20,811 --> 00:05:23,688
the commencement of the Urdr-Hunt
has been declared.

67
00:05:24,648 --> 00:05:25,982
The Urdr-Hunt is...

68
00:05:26,066 --> 00:05:29,194
a race in which those who possess
the qualifying Rings...

69
00:05:29,277 --> 00:05:34,616
travel between designated points
to collect specific data.

70
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:37,369
The grand prize is…

71
00:05:37,452 --> 00:05:38,870
100 billion Melia.

72
00:05:39,913 --> 00:05:41,998
An amount capable of...

73
00:05:42,082 --> 00:05:45,669
completely changing the life
of whoever obtains it.

74
00:05:58,306 --> 00:05:59,349
(Alert sound)

75
00:05:59,432 --> 00:06:00,267
Huh?

76
00:06:03,103 --> 00:06:04,396
(Alert sound)
(Renzie) Ah!

77
00:06:06,231 --> 00:06:07,899
(Coronal)
Dreams left unfulfilled…

78
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:10,318
ideals… desires…

79
00:06:11,403 --> 00:06:15,407
A vast fortune capable of pulling
all of them into reality.

80
00:06:16,032 --> 00:06:17,158
If that is the case…

81
00:06:20,495 --> 00:06:25,417
then perhaps it is inevitable
that the struggle surrounding it...

82
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,627
would become one fought
with lives at stake.

83
00:06:31,298 --> 00:06:32,382
Haa…

83.2
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,700
Small Transport Ship Erda-Maru II

84
00:06:39,014 --> 00:06:40,223
{\an8}(Wistario)
How is it?

85
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,476
Did you figure out
what’s written on the Ring?

86
00:06:43,977 --> 00:06:46,646
It appears to be
some sort of code…

87
00:06:46,730 --> 00:06:49,107
Unfortunately,
I cannot decipher it.

88
00:06:49,649 --> 00:06:51,067
I see…

89
00:06:51,359 --> 00:06:53,695
If it’s a ship from
the Calamity War era...

90
00:06:53,778 --> 00:06:56,907
maybe the data is connected
to that time period…

91
00:06:58,366 --> 00:07:01,953
(Coronal)
A message has arrived
from my master “N.”

92
00:07:02,037 --> 00:07:02,871
(Wistario)
What!?

93
00:07:03,622 --> 00:07:05,749
(Applause)

94
00:07:05,832 --> 00:07:07,667
Graturatio.

95
00:07:07,751 --> 00:07:10,086
You have cleared
the first mission of the Urdr-Hunt...

96
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:11,504
successfully.

97
00:07:11,588 --> 00:07:14,007
(Wistario)
Huh? That was it?

98
00:07:16,426 --> 00:07:18,220
(Coronal)
Within the Urdr-Hunt,

99
00:07:18,303 --> 00:07:23,433
an encounter with a rival means
a struggle for one another’s lives.

100
00:07:23,934 --> 00:07:26,269
In a sense,
that is the truth.

101
00:07:26,895 --> 00:07:27,938
However…

102
00:07:29,731 --> 00:07:32,400
(598)
Who the hell are you calling pirates!?

103
00:07:32,484 --> 00:07:34,444
(Wistario)
You attacked a merchant ship
with Mobile Suits...

104
00:07:34,527 --> 00:07:36,905
no matter how you look at it,
that makes you pirates!

105
00:07:40,367 --> 00:07:43,912
(598)
Don’t lump us in
with some cheap small-timers!

106
00:07:43,995 --> 00:07:47,916
Someday, we’re gonna become
the next Tekkadan!

107
00:07:48,458 --> 00:07:49,542
Tekkadan!?

108
00:07:49,626 --> 00:07:50,919
Did you just say Tekkadan!?

109
00:07:52,295 --> 00:07:53,755
Yeah, I did!

110
00:07:53,838 --> 00:07:56,341
We’re gonna become
the next Tekkadan!

111
00:07:56,424 --> 00:07:57,550
Hmph!

112
00:07:58,218 --> 00:08:00,387
(Wistario)
Don’t screw around with me!

113
00:08:01,721 --> 00:08:04,599
When did they ever
make a name for themselves

114
00:08:04,683 --> 00:08:07,602
by pulling pirate crap like this!?

115
00:08:08,561 --> 00:08:09,604
Guh…

116
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:14,025
(Coronal)
There were times when,
after clashing with everything at stake...

117
00:08:14,109 --> 00:08:17,946
strange bonds would be born
between people.

118
00:08:20,907 --> 00:08:22,784
(598)
Nngh… guh…
I’m fine…

119
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:27,038
(144 and others)
Waaaaah!

120
00:08:27,122 --> 00:08:28,456
(Kimbal)
Who the hell are you!?

121
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:30,000
(Impact sound)
(Kimbal)
Whoa!

122
00:08:32,085 --> 00:08:35,505
Man, there’s just something
about you guys that pisses me off!

123
00:08:41,094 --> 00:08:43,138
(598)
Guess I owe you one.

124
00:08:43,221 --> 00:08:44,514
Thanks.

125
00:08:44,597 --> 00:08:48,435
(Wistario)
It’s fine.
I just stuck my nose into it on my own.

126
00:08:48,810 --> 00:08:50,437
(598)
Heh. Fair enough.

127
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:55,984
(Wistario)
So what are you gonna do now?

128
00:08:56,901 --> 00:09:01,781
If you’ve got nowhere to go,
I could hire you over on Venus.

129
00:09:01,865 --> 00:09:02,741
Venus?

130
00:09:03,658 --> 00:09:05,618
With the prize money
from the Urdr-Hunt...

131
00:09:05,702 --> 00:09:08,705
I’m gonna buy back
my home colony, Radonitsa!

132
00:09:08,788 --> 00:09:11,082
Huh? Wait… what?
Buy it back?

133
00:09:11,166 --> 00:09:12,167
A colony!?

134
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:13,084
(Wistario)
Yeah!

135
00:09:14,669 --> 00:09:18,006
(Wistario)
Right now, that beautiful planet
only gets prisoners sent there...

136
00:09:18,089 --> 00:09:19,591
but I’m gonna turn it into a place...

137
00:09:20,175 --> 00:09:22,177
people from everywhere
actually want to visit.

138
00:09:22,552 --> 00:09:25,972
And for that,
I’m gonna need a lot of help.

139
00:09:26,431 --> 00:09:27,474
Mm…

140
00:09:29,768 --> 00:09:32,479
You’re already acting
like you’ve won the Urdr-Hunt.

141
00:09:32,562 --> 00:09:33,855
(Wistario)
Hm?

142
00:09:33,938 --> 00:09:35,148
(598)
Sorry, but…

143
00:09:35,231 --> 00:09:37,484
I don’t think it’s gonna be
that easy.

144
00:09:40,153 --> 00:09:41,321
(Wistario)
Then I guess
that can’t be helped.

145
00:09:41,404 --> 00:09:42,238
Yeah!

146
00:09:42,739 --> 00:09:45,784
Next time we meet,
you’re my rival.

147
00:09:45,867 --> 00:09:49,954
I won’t hold back,
so be ready, Wistario Afam!

148
00:09:50,038 --> 00:09:52,665
Same to you, 598.

149
00:09:53,458 --> 00:09:54,292
Yeah.

150
00:09:54,376 --> 00:09:55,960
See ya!

151
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:59,297
(Coronal)
598 and his companions.

152
00:10:00,006 --> 00:10:04,552
Deceived by the pirate Kimbal
and used as his underlings...

153
00:10:04,636 --> 00:10:07,430
they followed Wistario’s advice...

154
00:10:07,514 --> 00:10:10,058
and reclaimed ownership
of their Rings.

155
00:10:10,558 --> 00:10:14,145
They then officially joined
the Urdr-Hunt.

156
00:10:17,941 --> 00:10:23,363
And through all of that,
another important meeting took place…

157
00:10:23,446 --> 00:10:27,534
(Eating sounds)

158
00:10:27,617 --> 00:10:31,704
(Eating sounds)

159
00:10:31,788 --> 00:10:33,081
Who’s there!?

160
00:10:35,917 --> 00:10:36,960
Ah...

161
00:10:38,503 --> 00:10:39,337
Hm?

162
00:10:40,088 --> 00:10:43,216
You were on Kimbal’s ship…

163
00:10:44,384 --> 00:10:45,718
(Swallowing)

164
00:10:45,802 --> 00:10:47,095
(Cature)
Don’t call me “you.”

165
00:10:47,846 --> 00:10:48,972
I’m Cature.

166
00:10:49,931 --> 00:10:52,475
Cature Inoshee.

167
00:10:57,897 --> 00:11:00,984
(Muffled voice)
Hold on, let me finish eating this first.

168
00:11:03,194 --> 00:11:04,362
(Clapping)

169
00:11:04,445 --> 00:11:08,366
(Coronal)
Cature, who had been held captive
as cargo aboard the pirate ship...

170
00:11:08,449 --> 00:11:13,371
became a new member
of Wistario’s crew.

171
00:11:13,872 --> 00:11:17,458
The fact that he gained
a female companion his own age...

172
00:11:17,542 --> 00:11:19,750
was something
that delighted me as well.

172.2
00:11:19,751 --> 00:11:22,800
Falk Family Private Vessel
Cocoon Nidhoggr

173
00:11:21,171 --> 00:11:23,798
{\an8}And then,
there was one more…

174
00:11:23,882 --> 00:11:24,632
{\an8}(Renzie)
Guh…

175
00:11:28,678 --> 00:11:29,762
Huh!? What is that!?

176
00:11:29,846 --> 00:11:30,847
(Alert sound)

177
00:11:36,186 --> 00:11:37,937
(Andy)
What the hell are these things!?

178
00:11:38,021 --> 00:11:38,855
Gwah!

179
00:11:38,938 --> 00:11:41,399
Mr. Cyclase!
What the hell is going on!?

180
00:11:41,482 --> 00:11:43,443
(Cyclase)
The Cocoon’s automated defense system.

181
00:11:43,526 --> 00:11:44,360
Huh!?

182
00:11:44,861 --> 00:11:48,072
(Cyclase)
Once activated,
it deploys a massive number of unmanned craft...

183
00:11:48,156 --> 00:11:52,368
a system from the Calamity War era
designed to eliminate enemies completely.

184
00:11:52,994 --> 00:11:57,624
Though apparently,
it can’t distinguish targets very well,
so it attacks everything in sight.

185
00:12:00,710 --> 00:12:03,630
What!? You activated this thing!?

186
00:12:03,713 --> 00:12:05,298
(Cyclase)
I told you
I’d send reinforcements, didn’t I?

187
00:12:05,381 --> 00:12:06,216
(Renzie)
Ah!

188
00:12:06,299 --> 00:12:09,135
(Cyclase)
And let me warn you,
trying to stop the system is pointless.

189
00:12:09,219 --> 00:12:13,723
Damn it…
So we were expendable from the start!?

190
00:12:14,974 --> 00:12:16,392
(Andy)
More of them are coming!

191
00:12:19,354 --> 00:12:22,315
Boss! We’ll buy you some time!

192
00:12:22,398 --> 00:12:24,359
(Bito)
You make sure you get out alive!

193
00:12:24,442 --> 00:12:27,820
You idiots…
Stop it…

194
00:12:31,449 --> 00:12:32,492
(Andy)
We already decided this.

195
00:12:32,575 --> 00:12:33,701
(Impact sound)
(Andy)
Guh…

196
00:12:33,785 --> 00:12:35,870
We’re not gonna keep
getting rescued forever.

197
00:12:35,954 --> 00:12:39,874
Next time, we’re gonna save you
and finally look cool doing it!

198
00:12:39,958 --> 00:12:41,042
(Bito)
You still gotta build...

199
00:12:41,125 --> 00:12:44,379
the paradise
you promised us!

200
00:12:44,462 --> 00:12:46,297
That was the deal!

201
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,759
Cut it out… you idiots…

202
00:12:51,594 --> 00:12:53,513
Uooooooh!

203
00:12:56,099 --> 00:12:57,767
(Bito)
It’s the Renzie Squad!

204
00:12:57,850 --> 00:12:59,727
Don’t underestimate us!

205
00:13:00,395 --> 00:13:01,437
(Bito)
Gah!

206
00:13:02,730 --> 00:13:04,148
Ugh!

207
00:13:04,232 --> 00:13:05,275
Gah…

208
00:13:06,859 --> 00:13:08,152
(Explosion)

209
00:13:08,236 --> 00:13:09,904
Bito!

210
00:13:14,742 --> 00:13:16,411
(Renzie)
Stop it!

211
00:13:16,494 --> 00:13:17,662
Bito! Andy!

212
00:13:21,124 --> 00:13:24,669
Boss…
we told you to run…

213
00:13:27,588 --> 00:13:28,923
Guh…

214
00:13:29,007 --> 00:13:30,883
How could I run
and leave you behind!?

215
00:13:30,967 --> 00:13:33,386
Heh… you can’t do that…

216
00:13:33,469 --> 00:13:35,638
That was the promise… right…?

217
00:13:36,306 --> 00:13:38,224
(Andy)
Boss… you can’t die in…

218
00:13:38,308 --> 00:13:39,142
Ah…

219
00:13:40,018 --> 00:13:42,145
a… place… like…

220
00:13:42,228 --> 00:13:43,688
Andy!

221
00:13:44,856 --> 00:13:45,690
(Explosion)

222
00:13:45,773 --> 00:13:47,317
Cyclase, you bastard!

223
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,193
(Andy) Boss…
(Renzie) Guh!

224
00:13:49,277 --> 00:13:50,987
(Andy) We’re counting on you…
(Renzie) Ghh!

225
00:13:51,070 --> 00:13:54,490
(Andy)
For me… and Bito… too…

226
00:13:54,574 --> 00:13:55,700
(Impact sound)
(Renzie) Gah!

227
00:13:58,870 --> 00:14:01,831
Ugh…
Cyclase…

228
00:14:02,373 --> 00:14:04,375
I won’t… forgive…

229
00:14:10,381 --> 00:14:11,215
(Wistario)
Hey!

230
00:14:11,299 --> 00:14:13,968
Are you okay!?
Hey!

231
00:14:14,052 --> 00:14:15,094
Hey!

232
00:14:16,262 --> 00:14:19,349
(Coronal)
Though he belonged
to a rival organization...

233
00:14:19,432 --> 00:14:23,019
he was betrayed by his superior
and lost his comrades...

234
00:14:23,102 --> 00:14:25,313
Renzie Dablisco.

235
00:14:26,105 --> 00:14:28,274
I’m not dropping out
of the Urdr-Hunt.

236
00:14:29,317 --> 00:14:32,278
I still haven’t achieved my dream.

237
00:14:32,362 --> 00:14:35,907
The Urdr-Hunt
is my greatest chance.

238
00:14:36,449 --> 00:14:39,535
You mean that whole
“building a nation” thing?

239
00:14:39,952 --> 00:14:43,414
You’re willing to sacrifice your friends
for your own dream!?

240
00:14:43,998 --> 00:14:45,416
It’s not just my dream.

241
00:14:45,958 --> 00:14:47,418
It’s everyone’s dream!

242
00:14:48,169 --> 00:14:52,632
Right now, the Radonitsa Colony
doesn’t belong to any economic bloc.

243
00:14:52,715 --> 00:14:56,552
That means the people of Venus
don’t even have IDs.

244
00:14:57,637 --> 00:15:01,057
In other words,
they’re treated like nobodies.

245
00:15:01,641 --> 00:15:04,352
If we had our own nation,
we’d finally have a place to belong.

246
00:15:04,435 --> 00:15:07,480
We could proudly stand tall
as “the people of Venus.”

247
00:15:07,563 --> 00:15:10,566
It’s a dream meant
to make everyone happy.

248
00:15:10,650 --> 00:15:14,695
And with the Urdr-Hunt prize money,
I’m gonna make it happen.

249
00:15:18,366 --> 00:15:23,121
(Coronal)
In order to fulfill his own dream
and avenge his fallen comrades...

250
00:15:24,163 --> 00:15:28,626
Renzie decided to travel
alongside Wistario.

251
00:16:00,658 --> 00:16:01,492
(Incoming transmission)

252
00:16:01,576 --> 00:16:02,618
(Subordinate)
Boss.

253
00:16:04,078 --> 00:16:05,163
(Tamami)
What is it?

254
00:16:05,246 --> 00:16:07,331
(Subordinate)
We’ve located their ship.

255
00:16:07,874 --> 00:16:10,209
(Tamami)
Got it.
I’m heading over now.

256
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:13,713
(Palstai)
Ah!

257
00:16:14,297 --> 00:16:15,715
Who the hell are you?

258
00:16:15,798 --> 00:16:18,217
(Tamami)
Name’s Tamami Rakow.

259
00:16:18,301 --> 00:16:21,304
I’m the boss
of the Rakow Pirate Crew.

260
00:16:21,387 --> 00:16:23,848
(598)
I’m 598 of the Foundlings.

261
00:16:23,931 --> 00:16:25,975
What does a pirate want with us?

262
00:16:26,476 --> 00:16:30,980
We’ve got proof you brats attacked
a Teiwaz-registered cargo ship.

263
00:16:31,063 --> 00:16:33,566
I’m here to make you answer for it.

264
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:37,487
(Coronal)
Tamami Rakow,
one of the Ring holders...

265
00:16:38,196 --> 00:16:42,533
is the leader of the Rakow Pirate Crew
under the Turbines umbrella.

266
00:16:45,828 --> 00:16:47,997
Just spare the ship
and the Mobile Suits.

267
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:51,125
This place is our home,
and we need them to survive.

268
00:16:51,209 --> 00:16:52,668
We’ll pay compensation.

269
00:16:52,752 --> 00:16:55,880
And whatever we can’t cover now,
we’ll find a way to repay later.

270
00:16:55,963 --> 00:16:58,716
(Tamami)
Anyone can say that.

271
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:01,719
Then I’ll prove
it’s not just talk.

272
00:17:01,803 --> 00:17:04,138
What, you planning to chop off a finger?

273
00:17:05,723 --> 00:17:07,391
(598)
An entire arm.

274
00:17:07,475 --> 00:17:08,893
Huh?

275
00:17:08,976 --> 00:17:11,646
Right here, right now,
I’ll cut this arm off.

276
00:17:11,729 --> 00:17:12,897
(Palstai) Ah!
(Wistario) 598!?

277
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:13,814
(Renzie)
Hey! You…

278
00:17:13,898 --> 00:17:16,651
(598)
Then believe my words.

279
00:17:21,489 --> 00:17:22,406
Fine.

280
00:17:22,490 --> 00:17:23,658
(Tamami)
Let’s see you do it.

281
00:17:23,741 --> 00:17:24,659
(Palstai) Like hell we will…!
(Impact sound)

282
00:17:24,742 --> 00:17:26,661
(Alert sound)
(Wistario)
What now?

283
00:17:27,245 --> 00:17:30,456
(Rohm)
Ha-ha!
See that, Aiko!?

284
00:17:30,873 --> 00:17:35,294
(Rohm)
This great Rohm Zahn
is taking down every Ring holder at once!

285
00:17:35,378 --> 00:17:38,047
(Aiko)
Yeah, yeah.
You’re amazing, big bro.

286
00:17:38,130 --> 00:17:41,759
Seriously though,
we could’ve waited until after
they finished fighting each other…

287
00:17:41,842 --> 00:17:43,302
(Rohm)
Did you say something?

288
00:17:43,386 --> 00:17:45,221
(Aiko)
Big bro, you’re the best!

289
00:17:45,721 --> 00:17:49,225
(Coronal)
I was on edge worrying
about the fate of 598’s arm, but...

290
00:17:49,976 --> 00:17:54,647
after being attacked by a common enemy
and fighting back-to-back together...

291
00:17:54,730 --> 00:17:56,524
they managed
to reconcile for the moment.

292
00:17:57,066 --> 00:18:01,404
From then on,
598 and the others would work under Tamami...

293
00:18:01,487 --> 00:18:04,115
and learn the ways of business from her.

294
00:18:06,409 --> 00:18:09,328
Alright then,
who’s next!?

295
00:18:10,663 --> 00:18:11,497
Ah!

296
00:18:11,581 --> 00:18:15,585
(Rohm)
Behold!
The Gorgeous Pink and…

297
00:18:15,668 --> 00:18:18,170
the Gorgeous Silver…

298
00:18:18,254 --> 00:18:20,715
(Rohm & Aiko)
Brother Attack!

299
00:18:21,799 --> 00:18:23,467
Gwaaaaaah!

300
00:18:27,555 --> 00:18:29,098
(Rohm)
Aiko! Uwah!

301
00:18:29,181 --> 00:18:30,099
What...

302
00:18:30,182 --> 00:18:31,434
did you say!?

303
00:18:31,517 --> 00:18:33,603
(Rohm) Damn it all!

303.2
00:18:43,650 --> 00:18:46,150
Bauduin Family Orbital Satellite
Sleipnir Periphery

304
00:18:46,532 --> 00:18:49,201
(Coronal)
Not every Urdr-Hunt participant...

305
00:18:49,285 --> 00:18:54,040
is a seasoned fighter
capable of piloting a Mobile Suit.

306
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:56,125
Kozo Mendo is a...

307
00:18:56,208 --> 00:19:00,755
treasure hunter researching
the Calamity War said to have occurred...

308
00:19:00,838 --> 00:19:02,173
roughly 300 years ago.

309
00:19:02,256 --> 00:19:03,132
(Mendo) Yeah.

310
00:19:03,215 --> 00:19:04,800
That's right, young man.

311
00:19:04,884 --> 00:19:05,718
(Wistario) Hm?

312
00:19:05,801 --> 00:19:08,596
(Mendo) About your
Gundam Frame...

313
00:19:08,679 --> 00:19:09,555
Hajiroboshi?

314
00:19:09,639 --> 00:19:11,265
Yeah...

315
00:19:11,349 --> 00:19:13,392
There shouldn't be
any Gundam Frame...

316
00:19:13,476 --> 00:19:15,144
with a name like that.

317
00:19:15,227 --> 00:19:16,354
Huh?

318
00:19:16,437 --> 00:19:19,023
(Mendo)
What was your name again?

319
00:19:19,106 --> 00:19:22,568
Wistario Afam.
Try to remember it this time.

320
00:19:23,152 --> 00:19:26,197
Are you sure that's your real name?

321
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,490
Huh?

322
00:19:27,573 --> 00:19:30,368
(Mendo)
Once you learn Hajiroboshi's true name...

323
00:19:30,451 --> 00:19:34,038
you may no longer be able
to remain who you are now.

324
00:19:37,917 --> 00:19:40,378
(Coronal)
According to Mr. Mendo...

325
00:19:40,461 --> 00:19:42,880
every point indicated by the rings...

326
00:19:42,963 --> 00:19:45,883
is managed by one of the Seven Stars'
seven great houses...

327
00:19:45,966 --> 00:19:50,388
and consists of ruins or relics
dating back to the Calamity War.

328
00:19:52,390 --> 00:19:53,891
The Calamity War...

329
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:57,061
We Navigators are...

330
00:19:57,144 --> 00:20:01,649
beings tasked with guiding
ring-bearing participants...

331
00:20:02,316 --> 00:20:05,903
under the orders of our master "N,"
the organizer of the Urdr-Hunt...

332
00:20:07,029 --> 00:20:08,531
However...

333
00:20:09,573 --> 00:20:14,495
we have not been told anything
about the Urdr-Hunt's true purpose...

334
00:20:14,578 --> 00:20:16,789
or the nature of the data being collected.

335
00:20:17,289 --> 00:20:22,044
The connection between the Urdr-Hunt,
the Seven Stars, and the Calamity War...

336
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:24,672
Could it all really be true?

337
00:20:26,173 --> 00:20:29,176
Still, there have certainly been events...

338
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:31,429
{\an8}that make it hard to dismiss it all
as mere speculation...

339
00:20:31,512 --> 00:20:32,722
{\an8}(Iok) The Calamity War...

340
00:20:33,389 --> 00:20:37,476
(Iok) A mass-murder weapon
from the Calamity War... you say!?

341
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:41,063
And something like that
is inside territory overseen by House Kujan!?

342
00:20:41,772 --> 00:20:42,815
(Iok's Subordinate) Um...

343
00:20:42,898 --> 00:20:44,525
(Iok) How could I possibly allow...

344
00:20:44,608 --> 00:20:47,695
my precious subordinates
to remain exposed to such danger!?

345
00:20:48,070 --> 00:20:49,905
Suspend the investigation immediately!

346
00:20:49,989 --> 00:20:53,659
Inform the field team
to withdraw at once!

347
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:56,662
Until I personally arrive
to conduct the investigation...

348
00:20:56,746 --> 00:20:58,497
{\an8}the colony is to be sealed off!

349
00:20:59,832 --> 00:21:00,666
{\an8}(Gjallarhorn Soldier A)
Hey.

350
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:03,878
We've got orders from Lord Iok
to pull out immediately.

351
00:21:03,961 --> 00:21:05,546
(Gjallarhorn Soldier B)
Huh? Withdraw?

352
00:21:06,172 --> 00:21:09,133
What about this thing?
We're just leaving it here?

353
00:21:09,216 --> 00:21:11,552
(Gjallarhorn Soldier A) Can't be helped.
Those are the orders.

354
00:21:12,052 --> 00:21:14,889
{\an8}(Footsteps)

355
00:21:14,972 --> 00:21:15,890
{\an8}(Cyclase) Well then...

356
00:21:15,973 --> 00:21:18,559
{\an8}guess it's about time
I got back to work.

357
00:21:19,310 --> 00:21:21,562
(Cyclase)
It was fun talking with you.

358
00:21:21,645 --> 00:21:24,065
Yeah. Same here.

359
00:21:24,774 --> 00:21:25,816
Heh...

360
00:21:30,404 --> 00:21:31,280
Goodbye.

361
00:21:31,363 --> 00:21:32,573
(Ring glowing sound)
(Cyclase) Hm?

362
00:21:33,282 --> 00:21:35,826
(Spreading light sound)

363
00:21:41,791 --> 00:21:43,709
(Gjallarhorn Soldier A) Get back!

364
00:21:49,673 --> 00:21:51,217
(Wistario) That ring...

365
00:21:51,967 --> 00:21:53,719
You're an Urdr-Hunt participant.

366
00:21:54,261 --> 00:21:55,096
So you're...

367
00:21:55,179 --> 00:21:57,681
I've wanted to meet you
for quite some time.

368
00:21:57,765 --> 00:21:59,517
Wistario Afam.

369
00:22:00,351 --> 00:22:03,312
I was curious what kind of person
could single-handedly...

370
00:22:03,395 --> 00:22:05,856
wipe out Renzie's squad.

371
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:07,233
But I'm disappointed.

372
00:22:07,316 --> 00:22:09,151
So you're Cyclase!

373
00:22:10,027 --> 00:22:13,864
Turns out you're just some boring brat
lost in his own dreams.

374
00:22:15,825 --> 00:22:18,577
Well then, my business here is done.

375
00:22:19,745 --> 00:22:21,121
So this is goodbye.

376
00:22:21,205 --> 00:22:22,665
(Cyclase) Guh!
(Wistario) Ah!

377
00:22:24,834 --> 00:22:25,668
Damn...

378
00:22:26,335 --> 00:22:27,169
What is this!?

379
00:22:34,510 --> 00:22:35,636
Ah...

380
00:22:37,972 --> 00:22:41,183
(Coronal) Waiting for us
at the fourth point was...

381
00:22:41,267 --> 00:22:42,143
a Mobile Armor.

382
00:22:43,185 --> 00:22:46,063
A weapon of destruction
that triggered the Calamity War...

383
00:22:46,146 --> 00:22:51,402
300 years ago
and nearly drove humanity to extinction.

384
00:22:53,445 --> 00:22:54,905
(598) Boss! Hah!

385
00:23:16,260 --> 00:23:16,927
Ah!

386
00:23:19,513 --> 00:23:20,431
Damn it!

387
00:23:22,516 --> 00:23:24,059
What is this thing!?

388
00:23:24,143 --> 00:23:25,686
Why is it only reacting to Wistario!?

389
00:23:25,769 --> 00:23:26,604
Nngh...

390
00:23:26,687 --> 00:23:28,105
Huh!? What's this!?

391
00:23:29,565 --> 00:23:30,816
Hajiroboshi?

392
00:23:33,152 --> 00:23:35,237
No good... I can't control it...

393
00:23:39,909 --> 00:23:41,577
Guh... uh!

394
00:23:45,372 --> 00:23:48,000
Its power increased!? Ah!

395
00:23:51,170 --> 00:23:52,922
"Marchosias"?

396
00:24:53,357 --> 00:24:58,070
(Coronal) The battle
left us heavily damaged.

397
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:07,454
To carry out repairs and maintenance,
we decided to temporarily...

398
00:25:07,538 --> 00:25:11,875
return to the Radonitsa Colony
on Venus.

399
00:25:13,544 --> 00:25:15,796
Whoa... This is amazing!

400
00:25:16,630 --> 00:25:18,382
(598) Yeah, it's incredible, but...

401
00:25:18,465 --> 00:25:21,176
Does this really count as a colony?

402
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:22,928
I've never seen anything like this.

403
00:25:23,554 --> 00:25:26,682
This is my first time seeing
an open-type colony as well.

404
00:25:26,765 --> 00:25:30,561
It's different from both
the surface and closed colonies...

405
00:25:30,644 --> 00:25:34,440
This is definitely something
worth seeing for yourself.

406
00:25:35,065 --> 00:25:37,776
(Cature) It's really amazing...

407
00:25:38,527 --> 00:25:40,279
(Sound of wind)
(Cature) Heheheh...

408
00:25:40,362 --> 00:25:41,196
Ah!

409
00:25:42,322 --> 00:25:43,365
What's this?

410
00:25:44,074 --> 00:25:45,826
This is the best!

411
00:25:46,785 --> 00:25:49,705
Welcome to Radonitsa Colony!

412
00:25:56,086 --> 00:25:59,006
(Coronal)
It really is an incredible sight.

413
00:25:59,089 --> 00:26:02,843
(Cature) Yeah.
It makes me want to stay here forever.

414
00:26:02,926 --> 00:26:05,596
If you want to stay, Cature,
you can stay as long as you like.

415
00:26:05,679 --> 00:26:06,513
(Cature) Huh?

416
00:26:06,597 --> 00:26:08,098
(Wistario) You're welcome here.

417
00:26:08,182 --> 00:26:09,016
Ah...

418
00:26:09,892 --> 00:26:12,478
Of course, you'll have to help with work.

419
00:26:12,978 --> 00:26:14,021
You too, Coronal.

420
00:26:14,104 --> 00:26:14,772
(Coronal) Huh?

421
00:26:15,439 --> 00:26:17,066
Once the Urdr-Hunt is over...

422
00:26:17,149 --> 00:26:19,693
will you go back to that person called "N"?

423
00:26:19,777 --> 00:26:22,780
No, I don't have any such plans...

424
00:26:23,155 --> 00:26:25,032
A navigator's duty...

425
00:26:25,532 --> 00:26:28,535
lasts only until the
Urdr-Hunt comes to an end.

426
00:26:28,619 --> 00:26:29,661
(Wistario) Then...

427
00:26:29,745 --> 00:26:32,164
would you help me even after it's over?

428
00:26:32,247 --> 00:26:33,374
Ah...

429
00:26:35,292 --> 00:26:36,752
Would that really be alright?

430
00:26:36,835 --> 00:26:37,961
(Wistario) Of course.

431
00:26:38,045 --> 00:26:40,798
I want to keep drinking your tea,
Lady Coronal.

432
00:26:40,881 --> 00:26:42,049
Heh...

433
00:26:42,841 --> 00:26:44,426
Gratias.

434
00:26:44,510 --> 00:26:46,720
That makes me very happy.

435
00:26:46,804 --> 00:26:48,680
(Wistario) Right, Cature?

436
00:26:49,848 --> 00:26:50,682
Yeah.

437
00:26:51,308 --> 00:26:52,935
You too, 598 and Renzie!

438
00:26:53,018 --> 00:26:54,311
Once I buy the colony with the prize money...

439
00:26:54,395 --> 00:26:56,855
I told you,
I'm not handing over the prize money!

440
00:26:56,939 --> 00:26:58,816
(Renzie) Am I just an afterthought?
(Wistario) Ahahahaha!

441
00:26:59,316 --> 00:27:00,734
(598)
Quit laughing, damn it! Hey!

442
00:27:00,818 --> 00:27:01,944
(Cature) Yeah...

443
00:27:02,027 --> 00:27:03,570
I hope it can happen.

444
00:27:04,154 --> 00:27:04,988
(Coronal) Hm?

445
00:27:05,072 --> 00:27:06,073
(598) Hey! Wistario!

446
00:27:08,033 --> 00:27:10,577
(Sound of explosion)

447
00:27:16,333 --> 00:27:18,669
(Coronal)
While waiting for instructions
for the next point...

448
00:27:18,752 --> 00:27:21,797
there was some trouble with Gjallarhorn...

449
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:24,716
over the Mobile Suit
they had been hiding...

450
00:27:25,968 --> 00:27:27,803
(Isurugi) That hits a little close to home.

450.2
00:27:29,900 --> 00:27:32,850
Large Planetary Cruiser Saisei

451
00:27:31,849 --> 00:27:35,018
{\an8}(Coronal) Thanks to Ms. Tamami’s introduction,
598 was able to meet...

452
00:27:35,102 --> 00:27:39,773
the members of the Turbines
and Tekkadan that he admired so much...

453
00:27:45,737 --> 00:27:49,825
And somehow,
the amusing brothers who attacked us repeatedly...

454
00:27:49,908 --> 00:27:53,078
ended up forming
a bond of trust with us...

455
00:27:53,620 --> 00:27:56,039
Though there were occasional little disturbances...

456
00:27:56,123 --> 00:27:59,209
our peaceful days
continued on for a while...

457
00:27:59,293 --> 00:28:00,836
(Aiko) Ugh... Aaah...

458
00:28:01,462 --> 00:28:04,464
Ngh... Ugh... Aaah...

459
00:28:04,548 --> 00:28:08,635
Aaaahhh!
I'm sorry, big bro!

460
00:28:08,719 --> 00:28:10,971
Brotheeer!

461
00:28:11,513 --> 00:28:13,473
Come back, Aiko!

462
00:28:14,141 --> 00:28:17,978
(Rohm) Come baaack!
(Aiko) Big bro!

463
00:28:18,896 --> 00:28:20,981
(Coronal)
The great whirlpool...

464
00:28:21,064 --> 00:28:22,983
that would swallow us all...

465
00:28:24,026 --> 00:28:25,444
(Masked Man)
The name reported by Isurugi...

466
00:28:25,527 --> 00:28:27,070
as the person in charge...

467
00:28:27,154 --> 00:28:29,907
of the Afam facility was...

468
00:28:30,282 --> 00:28:32,034
Wistario Afam.

469
00:28:33,243 --> 00:28:34,119
A coincidence?

470
00:28:34,953 --> 00:28:36,121
Or perhaps...

471
00:28:36,914 --> 00:28:43,045
(Coronal) Meanwhile,
beneath the surface,
the ripples continued to spread little by little.

472
00:28:48,133 --> 00:28:49,593
Ah...

473
00:28:56,683 --> 00:28:59,603
(Renzie)
That's a Gjallarhorn Skipjack-class ship.

474
00:28:59,686 --> 00:29:02,105
First time I've ever seen one.

475
00:29:02,189 --> 00:29:04,274
That crest is?

476
00:29:04,608 --> 00:29:06,151
It's the Issue family's.

477
00:29:06,235 --> 00:29:08,111
Huh? One of the Seven Stars?

478
00:29:08,529 --> 00:29:09,363
Ngh...

479
00:29:10,614 --> 00:29:13,492
(Dexter)
Those bastards even brought out Mobile Suits.

480
00:29:13,575 --> 00:29:17,371
Six... seven...
Ugh, counting them is a pain.

481
00:29:17,454 --> 00:29:20,749
There's no way our forces
can handle an opponent like this.

482
00:29:20,832 --> 00:29:23,752
Guess we've got no choice
but to obey the order to stop...

483
00:29:24,086 --> 00:29:25,128
(Cature) No way...

484
00:29:26,129 --> 00:29:27,798
Absolutely not!

485
00:29:28,715 --> 00:29:29,633
Cature?

486
00:29:30,384 --> 00:29:32,344
I'd rather die than let them catch me...

487
00:29:32,427 --> 00:29:33,804
Ah...

488
00:29:33,887 --> 00:29:35,597
(Sound of door opening)
(Wistario) Cature!

489
00:29:37,266 --> 00:29:38,100
(Sound of incoming transmission)

490
00:29:38,183 --> 00:29:40,936
(Lond)
The ship over there, halt immediately.

491
00:29:41,019 --> 00:29:43,563
If you comply,
we won't resort to force.

492
00:29:44,189 --> 00:29:47,067
We are here concerning...

493
00:29:47,150 --> 00:29:49,569
a woman aboard your ship
named Cature Inoshee.

494
00:29:49,653 --> 00:29:50,487
What!?

495
00:29:50,570 --> 00:29:53,448
(Lond)
We ask that you promptly hand over Lady Cature.

496
00:29:53,532 --> 00:29:55,576
Lady... Cature?

497
00:29:56,243 --> 00:29:58,579
(Demnar)
Why would the Issue family?

498
00:30:04,167 --> 00:30:06,920
(Cature) Ngh... Ahh...

499
00:30:07,796 --> 00:30:09,548
Ngh... Nnnh...

500
00:30:09,631 --> 00:30:11,466
Ah... Ah... Ugh...

501
00:30:11,550 --> 00:30:13,051
Wah! Ah!

502
00:30:16,597 --> 00:30:17,639
Let go of me!

503
00:30:17,723 --> 00:30:18,807
Ah...

504
00:30:21,727 --> 00:30:24,062
(Wistario)
Even if you fight them, you can't win.

505
00:30:24,146 --> 00:30:26,440
(Cature)
Even so, if it's a choice between that and being captured...

506
00:30:26,523 --> 00:30:28,650
I'd rather die!

507
00:30:31,486 --> 00:30:33,822
(Wistario)
So they're really that awful, huh?

508
00:30:38,994 --> 00:30:40,245
Got it.

509
00:30:40,912 --> 00:30:42,331
Leave it to me.

510
00:30:42,414 --> 00:30:43,373
Huh? Wah!

511
00:30:47,878 --> 00:30:49,379
(Wistario)
I'll go in Hajiroboshi.

512
00:30:49,463 --> 00:30:51,423
Wistario...

513
00:30:51,506 --> 00:30:53,383
(Wistario)
Renzie, get ready!

514
00:30:53,467 --> 00:30:57,346
We're breaking through their blockade
and getting out of this sector!

515
00:30:57,763 --> 00:30:59,890
Damn it, guess we've got no choice!

516
00:31:00,474 --> 00:31:02,809
Things are about to get busy.

517
00:31:02,893 --> 00:31:04,394
I'll help with the preparations.

518
00:31:04,478 --> 00:31:06,229
Everyone...

519
00:31:06,730 --> 00:31:08,148
Thank you.

520
00:31:14,696 --> 00:31:15,614
Gah!

521
00:31:15,697 --> 00:31:17,240
(Coronal)
Against such a large force...

522
00:31:17,324 --> 00:31:20,702
we were at an overwhelming disadvantage, but...

523
00:31:20,786 --> 00:31:22,579
Its movements are completely different!

524
00:31:28,668 --> 00:31:29,503
(Masked Man)
Looks like...

525
00:31:30,253 --> 00:31:31,797
I made it in time.

526
00:31:33,548 --> 00:31:34,549
(Lond) Ngh!

527
00:31:34,633 --> 00:31:36,802
Now then, go.

528
00:31:36,885 --> 00:31:38,178
But...

529
00:31:38,261 --> 00:31:39,554
(Renzie) Wistario!

530
00:31:41,348 --> 00:31:43,809
(Coronal)
Thanks to the assistance of a man
calling himself Montag...

531
00:31:44,518 --> 00:31:47,521
we somehow managed to escape.

532
00:31:51,066 --> 00:31:53,985
Tch! It's not over yet!

533
00:31:59,741 --> 00:32:00,826
You bastard!

534
00:32:00,909 --> 00:32:03,161
(Masked Man)
Okina Uroka's ambition...

535
00:32:04,079 --> 00:32:06,540
You've noticed it too, haven't you?

536
00:32:07,207 --> 00:32:08,875
(Lond) What?
(Masked Man) Hmph.

537
00:32:14,047 --> 00:32:17,050
Who the hell was that guy?

538
00:32:19,803 --> 00:32:22,556
(Coronal)
Due to a certain incident on Earth...

539
00:32:22,639 --> 00:32:24,975
it seems the Issue family's heir...

540
00:32:25,058 --> 00:32:28,145
a woman named Carta Issue,
passed away.

541
00:32:28,812 --> 00:32:33,233
The current head of the family is elderly,
with little time remaining.

542
00:32:33,733 --> 00:32:37,988
The Issue family, desperate to choose a successor,
set their sights on...

543
00:32:38,071 --> 00:32:40,198
the family head's illegitimate child...

544
00:32:40,282 --> 00:32:41,992
Lady Cature.

545
00:32:43,577 --> 00:32:45,996
You don't intend to return
to the Issue family, do you, Cature?

546
00:32:46,079 --> 00:32:49,499
(Cature)
Return? That place was never my home!

547
00:32:50,584 --> 00:32:53,753
My mother was a servant
for the Issue family.

548
00:32:54,504 --> 00:32:57,340
After she became pregnant with me...

549
00:32:57,424 --> 00:33:01,720
the man who's supposedly my father
threw her away like a filthy rag!

550
00:33:01,803 --> 00:33:03,513
And now they want to take me back?

551
00:33:04,055 --> 00:33:06,099
I’ll never forgive them!

552
00:33:06,183 --> 00:33:07,934
（Coronal）
Cature...

553
00:33:08,310 --> 00:33:10,771
（Cature）
I don’t want to drag everyone into this...

554
00:33:11,354 --> 00:33:12,230
But!

555
00:33:12,314 --> 00:33:13,523
I understand.

556
00:33:14,399 --> 00:33:16,026
You don’t need to worry.

557
00:33:16,109 --> 00:33:19,362
I’ll never hand Cature over
to those bastards.

558
00:33:19,446 --> 00:33:20,739
（Demnar）
Young master...

559
00:33:22,157 --> 00:33:25,285
Cature is my precious friend...
my family.

560
00:33:25,994 --> 00:33:28,163
I’m not giving my family to anyone.

561
00:33:28,246 --> 00:33:29,080
（ring glowing）

562
00:33:29,164 --> 00:33:30,290
(Wistario）Huh?
(Coronal）Ah!

563
00:33:30,790 --> 00:33:32,792
（Wistario and the others）
Ah!

564
00:33:33,585 --> 00:33:34,794
The ring...

565
00:33:36,838 --> 00:33:37,798
{\an8}（Coronal）
The ring revealed...

566
00:33:37,881 --> 00:33:39,800
{\an8}the fifth point.

566.2
00:33:39,125 --> 00:33:42,375
Fareed Family Abandoned Battleship
Fenrir

567
00:33:40,050 --> 00:33:41,301
{\an8}However,
Mr. Wistario...

568
00:33:41,384 --> 00:33:42,719
{\an8}chose...

569
00:33:42,802 --> 00:33:46,973
to avoid heading there
in order to escape pursuit.

570
00:33:49,559 --> 00:33:52,479
{\an8}We slipped through
the Issue family's blockade…

570.2
00:33:49,300 --> 00:33:52,100
African Union Colony
Under Renovation

571
00:33:52,562 --> 00:33:56,858
dodging pursuers
as we continued to flee, but...

572
00:33:56,942 --> 00:33:59,110
eventually, the moment came...

573
00:34:03,156 --> 00:34:04,491
（Londo）
Unforgivable...

574
00:34:05,116 --> 00:34:09,079
To defile the purity
of the future head of the Issue family...

575
00:34:09,621 --> 00:34:10,497
I will not allow it!

576
00:34:10,580 --> 00:34:13,500
Further negotiations are pointless!

577
00:34:14,042 --> 00:34:17,504
We will recover Lady Cature
by force if necessary!

578
00:34:18,046 --> 00:34:22,509
Eliminate every member
of that ship’s crew!

579
00:34:22,592 --> 00:34:23,677
Yes, sir!

580
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:25,637
No! Stop!

581
00:34:26,471 --> 00:34:30,350
Wistario Afam!
I’ll warn you one last time.

582
00:34:30,433 --> 00:34:32,686
Hand over Lady Cature peacefully!

583
00:34:33,895 --> 00:34:34,729
No!

584
00:34:34,813 --> 00:34:36,231
Ghh...

585
00:34:37,524 --> 00:34:41,027
Then your comrades will lose their lives!

586
00:34:41,111 --> 00:34:42,654
Are you prepared for that!?

587
00:34:42,737 --> 00:34:44,406
（Wistario）
Of course I’m not!

588
00:34:45,657 --> 00:34:47,868
Don’t lay a hand on my friends!

589
00:34:47,951 --> 00:34:49,452
（Londo）
You brought this upon them!

590
00:34:50,078 --> 00:34:54,291
Lady Cature, or your comrades’ lives...
which will you choose!?

591
00:34:54,666 --> 00:34:55,709
（Wistario）
They’re all my family!

592
00:34:55,792 --> 00:34:56,459
（Coronal）
Cature!

593
00:34:56,543 --> 00:34:58,461
（Wistario）
There’s no way I can choose!

594
00:34:58,545 --> 00:35:02,173
I’ll say it again!
Don’t touch my family!

595
00:35:03,508 --> 00:35:05,218
Fool!

596
00:35:07,137 --> 00:35:09,681
Attention all deployed units!

597
00:35:09,764 --> 00:35:11,933
All personnel, eliminate these people at on...

598
00:35:12,017 --> 00:35:13,560
（Cature）
Stop it!

599
00:35:14,644 --> 00:35:16,271
Cature... Ah!

600
00:35:18,231 --> 00:35:20,859
Nobody move!

601
00:35:20,942 --> 00:35:22,277
（Coronal）
Cature!

602
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,987
（Londo）
La... Lady Cature!

603
00:35:24,529 --> 00:35:25,906
（Wistario）
Cature? What are you...

604
00:35:25,989 --> 00:35:26,740
（Cature）
I...

605
00:35:27,741 --> 00:35:29,492
I’ll go to the Issue family.

606
00:35:29,576 --> 00:35:30,619
So...

607
00:35:31,286 --> 00:35:32,787
please stop.

608
00:35:33,288 --> 00:35:35,457
（Wistario）
What are you saying, Cature?

609
00:35:35,957 --> 00:35:39,085
No! I won’t allow that!

610
00:35:41,546 --> 00:35:43,048
（Cature）
Wistario...

611
00:35:44,883 --> 00:35:46,051
Thank you.

612
00:35:47,052 --> 00:35:50,555
For protecting me
all the way to the very end.

613
00:35:51,765 --> 00:35:53,642
It made me so happy.

614
00:35:53,725 --> 00:35:56,686
Happy enough that
I could die right now...

615
00:35:56,770 --> 00:35:57,896
Ghh...

616
00:35:57,979 --> 00:35:58,813
（Cature）
So...

617
00:36:00,649 --> 00:36:01,983
your turn is over.

618
00:36:02,776 --> 00:36:07,113
Now it’s my turn
to protect you and everyone else.

619
00:36:08,490 --> 00:36:09,866
Because...

620
00:36:09,950 --> 00:36:12,619
that’s what family does, right?

621
00:36:13,662 --> 00:36:15,997
Ngh... ngh!

622
00:36:16,831 --> 00:36:17,999
Heh...

623
00:36:19,334 --> 00:36:20,543
（Wistario）
Cature...

624
00:36:21,836 --> 00:36:22,754
（Coronal）
For the sake of family...

625
00:36:23,838 --> 00:36:25,799
That’s what Cature said as she...

626
00:36:25,882 --> 00:36:28,802
left before our eyes.

627
00:36:30,595 --> 00:36:33,306
All of us shared one wish...

628
00:36:33,807 --> 00:36:35,350
We wanted Cature back!

629
00:36:36,518 --> 00:36:41,147
And for that,
we first had to find where she was.

630
00:36:41,940 --> 00:36:45,360
After gathering information
from various sources, we learned...

631
00:36:47,904 --> 00:36:50,490
that the current Issue family
had split into two factions...

632
00:36:50,573 --> 00:36:55,453
fighting over what should be done
with Cature.

633
00:36:57,288 --> 00:37:00,709
And that the man hired
by the opposing faction...

634
00:37:01,209 --> 00:37:04,713
to eliminate Londo Bron,
who had abducted Cature...

635
00:37:04,796 --> 00:37:07,882
was none other than
that Cyclase Myer.

636
00:37:13,930 --> 00:37:15,140
If we follow...

637
00:37:15,223 --> 00:37:18,226
the ship of Cyclase Myer,
whose location we’ve identified...

638
00:37:18,309 --> 00:37:21,312
then surely,
Cature will be waiting beyond it...

639
00:37:22,188 --> 00:37:24,190
Our course was set.

640
00:37:26,776 --> 00:37:27,902
（Cyclase）
I see.

641
00:37:27,986 --> 00:37:29,362
You certainly have skill.

642
00:37:29,446 --> 00:37:30,822
Your head is mine!

643
00:37:31,448 --> 00:37:33,450
（Tagging）
A little greeting to start us off!

644
00:37:35,118 --> 00:37:37,537
（naval bombardment）

645
00:37:49,674 --> 00:37:52,051
（door opens）

646
00:37:52,719 --> 00:37:54,596
（Coronal）
Can’t sleep?

647
00:37:54,679 --> 00:37:55,805
（Wistario）
Coronal...

648
00:37:58,975 --> 00:37:59,809
Sorry.

649
00:37:59,893 --> 00:38:01,269
（Coronal）
Hm?

650
00:38:01,352 --> 00:38:02,395
（Wistario）
Urdr-Hunt...

651
00:38:02,479 --> 00:38:05,565
Because I ended up
abandoning it partway through

652
00:38:07,776 --> 00:38:08,860
No

653
00:38:09,402 --> 00:38:14,365
I want to help Lady Cature too
we all feel the same

654
00:38:14,449 --> 00:38:15,700
And...

655
00:38:15,784 --> 00:38:19,871
it’s not like we’ve
already lost the Urdr-Hunt

656
00:38:19,954 --> 00:38:23,666
Even after we save Lady Cature,
we can still recover

657
00:38:23,750 --> 00:38:26,336
(Wistario) Yeah, you’re right

658
00:38:27,003 --> 00:38:30,590
So let’s definitely
get Lady Cature back

659
00:38:30,673 --> 00:38:33,176
Yeah, definitely

660
00:38:33,259 --> 00:38:34,093
So...

661
00:38:36,888 --> 00:38:37,806
(Coronal) Huh?

662
00:38:37,889 --> 00:38:39,682
(Wistario)
Until then... Lady Coronal...

663
00:38:39,766 --> 00:38:42,018
I want you to hold onto this ring

664
00:38:44,813 --> 00:38:45,855
Understood

665
00:38:49,109 --> 00:38:53,613
Until we get Lady Cature back,
I will keep it safe

666
00:38:54,405 --> 00:38:55,615
(Wistario) Thanks

667
00:38:58,201 --> 00:39:00,286
Hey, you old guys

668
00:39:00,370 --> 00:39:02,413
Eavesdropping isn’t cool

669
00:39:02,497 --> 00:39:03,623
(Dexter)
Then you should...

670
00:39:03,706 --> 00:39:06,376
just go back to your room already

671
00:39:06,459 --> 00:39:08,545
(Demnar)
You should be resting...

672
00:39:08,628 --> 00:39:10,088
the young master was concerned

673
00:39:11,214 --> 00:39:13,591
I can’t sleep anyway

674
00:39:13,675 --> 00:39:16,594
Ever since I heard
Cyclase is involved...

675
00:39:17,595 --> 00:39:19,097
Andy and Bito...

676
00:39:19,180 --> 00:39:23,017
their faces keep popping into my head
and won’t leave

677
00:39:23,393 --> 00:39:26,312
We’re going to save that girl

678
00:39:26,396 --> 00:39:28,106
You haven’t forgotten that, have you?

679
00:39:29,065 --> 00:39:32,026
Don’t lump me in
with senile old men

680
00:39:32,110 --> 00:39:34,112
Of course I remember

681
00:39:34,195 --> 00:39:37,240
But when I face that guy...

682
00:39:37,949 --> 00:39:41,744
I feel like my urge for revenge
is going to explode

683
00:39:41,828 --> 00:39:45,623
(Demnar) That man’s grudge
is your personal matter

684
00:39:46,583 --> 00:39:48,376
I won’t tell you not to take revenge

685
00:39:49,419 --> 00:39:50,587
Old man...

686
00:39:50,670 --> 00:39:53,131
(Demnar)
I’m sure the young master would say the same

687
00:39:53,214 --> 00:39:54,841
Yeah, he might

688
00:39:55,717 --> 00:39:57,886
(Renzie)
He even saved a guy like me...

689
00:39:57,969 --> 00:40:00,430
and let me board his ship

690
00:40:00,513 --> 00:40:03,516
On top of that, he even makes me help
with his dream...

691
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:06,102
I really don’t understand him

692
00:40:06,644 --> 00:40:09,105
But if it’s his dream...

693
00:40:09,189 --> 00:40:12,191
I oddly want to see it through myself

694
00:40:13,484 --> 00:40:14,777
But before that...

695
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:18,823
I want to settle things
with Cyclase

696
00:40:18,907 --> 00:40:20,742
(Demnar) Then go settle it

697
00:40:21,492 --> 00:40:23,494
Just don’t you die

698
00:40:24,287 --> 00:40:26,205
Yeah, I know

699
00:40:26,706 --> 00:40:29,000
(Demnar)
You’re also...

700
00:40:29,083 --> 00:40:31,586
a valuable worker who will carry
the future of Venus

701
00:40:31,669 --> 00:40:32,503
Heh.

702
00:40:32,587 --> 00:40:35,006
More importantly, the young master would grieve.

703
00:40:35,590 --> 00:40:41,012
I ain't planning on dying,
and I ain't planning on letting anyone else die either.

704
00:40:41,846 --> 00:40:44,641
I'm gonna settle everything
I left unfinished here...

705
00:40:45,141 --> 00:40:47,644
and from there on out,
all that's left is moving forward!

706
00:40:48,269 --> 00:40:51,564
Do not ever forget those words.

707
00:40:51,648 --> 00:40:54,984
Like hell we're dying before you geezers!

708
00:40:55,068 --> 00:40:56,653
（Sinister）Hmm~?

709
00:40:57,236 --> 00:40:59,572
Looks like something strange
just came into view.

710
00:40:59,656 --> 00:41:03,409
The only strange thing here
is your face, old man.

711
00:41:03,493 --> 00:41:05,536
Our faces are practically identical.

712
00:41:05,620 --> 00:41:06,537
What is it?

713
00:41:06,621 --> 00:41:08,539
（Sinister）
That's the ship we've been chasing.

714
00:41:08,623 --> 00:41:10,667
We caught up to Cyclase!?

715
00:41:11,542 --> 00:41:13,378
Let's go inform the young master.

716
00:41:18,007 --> 00:41:20,760
What the hell is this place?

717
00:41:27,058 --> 00:41:28,935
{\an8}（Coronal）
The Issue family's sacred ground...

718
00:41:29,018 --> 00:41:30,436
{\an8}Ratatoskr.

719
00:41:30,895 --> 00:41:36,234
Apparently it's an old-style power transmission system
that uses Ahab Reactors.

720
00:41:36,859 --> 00:41:39,862
Lond Bron, who took Cature with him...

721
00:41:39,946 --> 00:41:42,115
the forces of Cyclase Myer pursuing him...

722
00:41:42,824 --> 00:41:46,577
and Wistario and his companions
chasing after them in turn...

723
00:41:47,078 --> 00:41:49,706
The final battle is finally at hand!

724
00:41:51,124 --> 00:41:52,000
Hah!

725
00:41:53,668 --> 00:41:55,962
（Thunder rumbling）

726
00:41:56,045 --> 00:41:57,005
（Coronal）Ugh...

727
00:41:57,088 --> 00:41:58,214
That's...

728
00:41:59,007 --> 00:42:00,675
Hey, that light...

729
00:42:00,758 --> 00:42:02,427
（Sinister）Hm? Let's see...

730
00:42:02,510 --> 00:42:03,803
There we go.

731
00:42:04,220 --> 00:42:05,430
（Renzie）A Mobile Suit?

732
00:42:07,181 --> 00:42:08,433
Cyclase is out there too!

733
00:42:08,933 --> 00:42:10,685
He's caught up with Cature and the others.

734
00:42:10,768 --> 00:42:13,104
We're heading out too, Renzie.

735
00:42:13,521 --> 00:42:15,148
（Renzie）
I'm ending this here and now!

736
00:42:15,231 --> 00:42:16,065
（Door opens）

737
00:42:16,149 --> 00:42:17,442
(Coronal）Wistario.
(Wistario）Huh?

738
00:42:18,151 --> 00:42:19,444
Please be careful.

739
00:42:20,069 --> 00:42:22,447
I'll definitely bring Cature back!

740
00:42:23,156 --> 00:42:24,198
Yes!

741
00:42:28,578 --> 00:42:29,620
Young master...

742
00:43:26,052 --> 00:43:28,471
Renzie Dablisco, Asmoday.

743
00:43:29,055 --> 00:43:31,224
Wistario Afam, Hajiroboshi.

744
00:43:31,849 --> 00:43:33,434
(Wistario）Launching!
(Renzie）Let's go!

745
00:43:49,742 --> 00:43:52,745
（Coronal）The reason Lond Bron
came to Ratatoskr...

746
00:43:52,829 --> 00:43:55,123
wasn't just to resupply.

747
00:43:55,623 --> 00:43:58,543
It seems he also came
to obtain...

748
00:43:58,626 --> 00:43:59,919
a Mobile Suit passed down
through the Issue family line.

749
00:44:00,002 --> 00:44:00,670
Ah!

750
00:44:10,221 --> 00:44:11,222
Kyaa!

751
00:44:12,557 --> 00:44:15,476
To draw your bow against this Zagan...

752
00:44:16,978 --> 00:44:18,479
Learn your place!

753
00:44:25,278 --> 00:44:26,696
（Subordinate A）Uwaaah!

754
00:44:41,669 --> 00:44:42,587
Hmph.

755
00:44:43,671 --> 00:44:44,839
（Subordinate B）Ngh! Guh...

756
00:44:53,556 --> 00:44:54,640
Gah!

757
00:45:02,148 --> 00:45:03,065
Kyaaah!

758
00:45:05,151 --> 00:45:06,444
（Warning alarm）
（Wistario）Ah!

759
00:45:14,410 --> 00:45:15,244
So you've come.

760
00:45:15,328 --> 00:45:17,413
（Lond）Wistario Afam.

761
00:45:17,497 --> 00:45:18,748
（Wistario）
So it was you after all.

762
00:45:19,373 --> 00:45:21,584
You're giving Cature back!

763
00:45:22,960 --> 00:45:24,045
（Incoming transmission）

764
00:45:24,128 --> 00:45:25,630
（598）Wistario!

765
00:45:26,839 --> 00:45:28,382
I'll give you a hand!

766
00:45:33,054 --> 00:45:33,888
（Cyclase）Well?

767
00:45:35,056 --> 00:45:36,307
（Batch）We've arrived.

768
00:45:36,390 --> 00:45:37,683
Beginning the operation now.

769
00:45:37,767 --> 00:45:38,601
I'm counting on you.

770
00:45:38,684 --> 00:45:40,394
（Warning alarm）
（Cyclase）Hm! So they've come.

771
00:45:41,771 --> 00:45:44,148
（Cyclase）
We'll deal with these annoying flies.

772
00:45:44,649 --> 00:45:45,900
（Tagging）Okaaay.

773
00:45:49,987 --> 00:45:52,657
Yo. I've been wanting to see you.

774
00:45:53,491 --> 00:45:54,909
（Renzie）Cyclase!

775
00:45:55,993 --> 00:45:59,914
So you're still alive,
Renzie Dablisco.

776
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:02,750
You're the one bastard I won't forgive!

777
00:46:02,833 --> 00:46:08,172
For Andy and Bito's sake,
I'm taking my revenge right here!

778
00:46:16,180 --> 00:46:18,683
（Lond）I'm still not done!

779
00:46:22,353 --> 00:46:23,980
Guh... Ghk!

780
00:46:26,065 --> 00:46:26,983
Ngh!

781
00:46:37,076 --> 00:46:40,288
(Lond）UOOOOOOHHHH!
(Wistario）Ah!

782
00:46:41,872 --> 00:46:43,291
（598）Wistario!

783
00:46:46,002 --> 00:46:47,169
（Lond）Guh...

784
00:46:47,878 --> 00:46:52,300
I am the one who must protect that person!

785
00:47:00,600 --> 00:47:01,851
Gah...

786
00:47:13,112 --> 00:47:15,406
（598）Is it... over?

787
00:47:17,867 --> 00:47:19,118
No. Not yet.

788
00:47:19,827 --> 00:47:22,371
Hang on, Cature! I'm coming!

789
00:47:32,965 --> 00:47:34,633
Guh... Ah!

790
00:47:35,801 --> 00:47:37,636
（Renzie）
Damn it! Stop darting around!

791
00:47:37,720 --> 00:47:40,389
Quit running away, Cyclase!

792
00:47:40,473 --> 00:47:41,557
Hmph...

793
00:47:42,266 --> 00:47:43,392
It's about time.

794
00:47:43,893 --> 00:47:46,896
（Impact sound）
（Renzie）Ah! What the hell!?

795
00:47:48,898 --> 00:47:51,651
Looks like Batch fulfilled her role.

796
00:47:51,734 --> 00:47:54,653
Well, we are exceptionally capable.

797
00:47:56,739 --> 00:47:58,658
This was your doing!?

798
00:47:59,325 --> 00:48:00,159
（Cyclase）Now then...

799
00:48:00,826 --> 00:48:03,913
the beginning of true freedom.

800
00:48:03,996 --> 00:48:05,289
What's happening!?

801
00:48:05,373 --> 00:48:06,415
(Impact sound)
(Renzie) Grrh!

802
00:48:16,467 --> 00:48:17,676
(Coronal) Kyaah!

803
00:48:18,302 --> 00:48:19,512
Lady Coronal!

804
00:48:19,595 --> 00:48:20,429
Ah!

805
00:48:20,513 --> 00:48:21,931
(Coronal) Ah!

806
00:48:23,599 --> 00:48:24,433
That's...

807
00:48:25,059 --> 00:48:26,435
(Coronal) The ring...

808
00:48:27,103 --> 00:48:29,188
(Palstie)
Is it writing data?

809
00:48:30,564 --> 00:48:33,651
(Mendo) Ratatoskr is
a place tied to the Issue family.

810
00:48:33,734 --> 00:48:35,194
So this really was...

811
00:48:35,694 --> 00:48:38,239
the sixth point.

812
00:48:38,572 --> 00:48:41,158
(Slice)
But why now?

813
00:48:48,165 --> 00:48:49,208
(Pilot) Hurry!

814
00:48:49,291 --> 00:48:51,585
{\an8}They're catching up to us!
What happened to Captain Lond!?

815
00:48:51,669 --> 00:48:52,962
{\an8}(Co-pilot)
We can't contact him!

816
00:48:54,171 --> 00:48:55,714
(Cature) Wistario...

817
00:48:58,259 --> 00:49:00,720
(598)
It'll be trouble if they board our ship!

818
00:49:00,803 --> 00:49:01,637
Cature...

819
00:49:01,720 --> 00:49:03,722
(Impact sound)
(Wistario) Ah! What was that!?

820
00:49:19,572 --> 00:49:21,157
(Demnar) An optical weapon?

821
00:49:21,240 --> 00:49:23,492
(Dexter)
Just how big is that thing?

822
00:49:26,912 --> 00:49:27,747
(Slice) Ah!

823
00:49:27,830 --> 00:49:29,749
What in the world is that?

824
00:49:30,416 --> 00:49:31,250
Ah...

825
00:49:34,086 --> 00:49:35,754
What the hell is that!?

826
00:49:54,148 --> 00:49:55,441
It's awakened...

827
00:49:56,317 --> 00:49:58,068
The Mobile Armor...

828
00:50:02,865 --> 00:50:05,409
Hah! What is this thing?

829
00:50:05,493 --> 00:50:06,744
(Sound of incoming transmission)
(Wistario) Hm?

830
00:50:06,827 --> 00:50:10,164
(Demnar) Young master, that thing
is a Mobile Armor!

831
00:50:10,247 --> 00:50:12,625
(Wistario)
A Mobile Armor!? This is?

832
00:50:12,708 --> 00:50:14,293
They're really this huge?

833
00:50:14,376 --> 00:50:17,296
Sorry. A little farewell gift from Cyclase.

834
00:50:17,838 --> 00:50:19,798
What're we gonna do, Wistario!?

835
00:50:22,009 --> 00:50:23,385
Cature's up ahead.

836
00:50:24,053 --> 00:50:26,305
If you're gonna stand in my way...

837
00:50:27,973 --> 00:50:29,683
{\an8}Then I'll crush you and move on!

838
00:50:45,032 --> 00:50:46,867
(Coronal) A Mobile Armor...

839
00:50:46,951 --> 00:50:50,955
Unlike the wreckage from past battles,
this one was fully intact.

840
00:50:51,455 --> 00:50:53,791
Its destructive power
was overwhelming.

841
00:50:53,874 --> 00:50:54,959
(Impact sound)
(Renzie) Guh!

842
00:50:55,459 --> 00:50:58,879
(Coronal) The other members of the
Urdr-Hunt also rushed in one after another...

843
00:50:59,255 --> 00:51:01,966
and it became a battle for survival...

844
00:51:05,052 --> 00:51:06,637
Ngh! Again!?

845
00:51:06,720 --> 00:51:08,472
(Warning alarm)
(Wistario) Ah!

846
00:51:14,770 --> 00:51:15,980
(Wistario) 598!

847
00:51:16,063 --> 00:51:19,900
Wooooooooooah!

848
00:51:23,195 --> 00:51:24,238
Sorry to keep you waiting!

849
00:51:30,327 --> 00:51:31,245
Drop dead!

850
00:51:31,328 --> 00:51:32,746
(Warning alarm)
(Tamami) Huh!?

851
00:51:37,459 --> 00:51:39,253
Yo, brother!

852
00:51:39,336 --> 00:51:40,754
Sorry to keep ya waiting!

853
00:51:48,470 --> 00:51:50,014
(Wistario) Everyone!

854
00:51:50,097 --> 00:51:51,098
Did we get it?

855
00:51:51,181 --> 00:51:52,016
Ah...

856
00:51:53,100 --> 00:51:53,767
Ngh!

857
00:51:58,939 --> 00:51:59,773
(Tamami) Ah!

858
00:52:00,733 --> 00:52:01,775
(Aiko & Roam) Whoa!

859
00:52:06,113 --> 00:52:07,531
That's...

860
00:52:07,615 --> 00:52:09,033
That's the main body?

861
00:52:09,116 --> 00:52:10,367
Ngh!

862
00:52:12,870 --> 00:52:13,787
Huh?

863
00:52:16,915 --> 00:52:18,626
(Wistario)
This is like back then...

864
00:52:18,709 --> 00:52:21,337
Marcho... sias?

865
00:52:24,548 --> 00:52:26,967
(Coronal)
In the end, the deciding factor was...

866
00:52:27,051 --> 00:52:28,928
once again, the activation of...

867
00:52:29,011 --> 00:52:32,932
Hajiroboshi's mysterious
power-up ability.

868
00:52:35,142 --> 00:52:37,811
Ugh! Ugh! Uuuugh!

869
00:52:46,153 --> 00:52:47,571
Ugh...

870
00:52:47,655 --> 00:52:48,572
Ah!

871
00:52:56,538 --> 00:52:58,165
(598) Amazing...

872
00:53:00,918 --> 00:53:03,837
Hah... Hah... Hah...

873
00:53:11,845 --> 00:53:14,223
Is this...
the end?

874
00:53:14,306 --> 00:53:16,350
Yeah... looks like it.

875
00:53:17,226 --> 00:53:19,853
(Renzie)
Even I can't move anymore...

876
00:53:30,197 --> 00:53:35,285
So you weren't the freedom
I had been searching for either...

877
00:53:36,995 --> 00:53:39,623
Still, well...

878
00:53:43,794 --> 00:53:46,088
(Wistario)
That's right! What about Cature!?

879
00:53:47,214 --> 00:53:48,132
(Coronal) Wistario!

880
00:53:48,924 --> 00:53:51,719
The launch carrying Cature
has been swept away!

881
00:53:51,802 --> 00:53:55,347
At this rate, it'll be pulled
into the lightning storm!

882
00:54:00,853 --> 00:54:02,062
Cature!

883
00:54:02,146 --> 00:54:04,022
Hurry, Wistario!

884
00:54:16,493 --> 00:54:17,995
Wistario...

885
00:54:25,294 --> 00:54:26,920
(Coronal) Lady Cature

886
00:54:37,222 --> 00:54:39,850
(Sinister)
16,000 meters to target!

887
00:54:39,933 --> 00:54:41,935
(Dexter)
Just a little more!

888
00:54:42,019 --> 00:54:43,395
Young master...

889
00:54:45,689 --> 00:54:47,441
Hah! Ngh!

890
00:54:50,444 --> 00:54:51,528
Go!

891
00:54:51,612 --> 00:54:53,906
Wistario!

892
00:55:01,246 --> 00:55:02,664
Ah...

893
00:55:03,791 --> 00:55:05,125
No...

894
00:55:05,209 --> 00:55:06,543
Ngh...

895
00:55:08,295 --> 00:55:09,880
No way...

896
00:55:10,964 --> 00:55:12,633
(Sinister) The launch's signal...

897
00:55:12,716 --> 00:55:14,384
has disappeared...

898
00:55:15,219 --> 00:55:18,222
(Demnar)
We... didn't make it...

899
00:55:20,557 --> 00:55:21,391
Ah...

900
00:55:21,475 --> 00:55:23,227
No! Not yet!

901
00:55:23,310 --> 00:55:24,144
(Demnar and the others) Huh!?

902
00:55:24,228 --> 00:55:27,648
(Signal beeping)

903
00:55:34,363 --> 00:55:35,239
Mm...

904
00:55:40,494 --> 00:55:41,370
Hah!

905
00:56:05,644 --> 00:56:07,771
Cature! Why!?

906
00:56:08,188 --> 00:56:11,441
No matter how dangerous the place was,
you always came after me

907
00:56:12,067 --> 00:56:16,488
So I knew...
I had to return to you, Wistario...

908
00:56:18,407 --> 00:56:19,825
Wistario...

909
00:56:20,367 --> 00:56:21,618
I...

910
00:56:23,162 --> 00:56:25,831
(Wistario) Cature!
Let's be happy together!

911
00:56:27,332 --> 00:56:28,417
(Cature) Yeah!

912
00:56:47,477 --> 00:56:50,314
(Coronal)
Lady Cature came back to us

913
00:56:51,064 --> 00:56:55,027
And once again,
we became one

914
00:56:58,280 --> 00:56:59,239
Phew...

915
00:56:59,323 --> 00:57:00,741
(Knocking)

916
00:57:00,824 --> 00:57:01,658
Yes?

917
00:57:01,742 --> 00:57:02,576
(Door opens)

918
00:57:02,659 --> 00:57:04,286
(Coronal) Lady Cature

919
00:57:04,369 --> 00:57:06,163
What were you doing?

920
00:57:06,246 --> 00:57:10,042
I was rereading
the journal entries I've written.

921
00:57:10,125 --> 00:57:11,293
I see

922
00:57:11,627 --> 00:57:13,712
Hey, want to step outside for a bit?

923
00:57:13,795 --> 00:57:15,339
(Coronal) Heh...

924
00:57:15,422 --> 00:57:16,548
Yes

925
00:57:17,341 --> 00:57:20,761
(Coronal)
What is it that people desire?

926
00:57:21,595 --> 00:57:24,181
Within the ordinary lives
we lived until yesterday...

927
00:57:24,264 --> 00:57:29,186
When suddenly, an unexpected door of fate
appears before us...

928
00:57:29,770 --> 00:57:32,189
Our lives... our futures...

929
00:57:33,398 --> 00:57:38,403
When beyond that door,
we glimpse a light powerful enough
to change everything...

930
00:57:39,988 --> 00:57:44,409
The 100 billion Melia prize
has yet to be claimed.

931
00:57:44,993 --> 00:57:46,203
And yet...

932
00:57:46,662 --> 00:57:52,084
I'm certain that something even more precious
than immeasurable wealth lies here...

933
00:57:53,001 --> 00:57:57,130
The irreplaceable treasure
of the people we meet.

934
00:58:00,258 --> 00:58:01,468
(Coronal) Here...

935
00:58:01,760 --> 00:58:05,806
I planned to return it
once we returned to Venus and settled in.

936
00:58:05,889 --> 00:58:08,475
There hasn't been any reaction
since last time, right?

937
00:58:08,558 --> 00:58:09,851
(Coronal) Correct

938
00:58:09,935 --> 00:58:13,021
However, "N" instructed us
to remain on standby.

939
00:58:13,105 --> 00:58:17,025
A message was sent directly to me
as the navigator...

940
00:58:17,526 --> 00:58:20,362
Then the Urdr-Hunt
is still continuing

941
00:58:20,862 --> 00:58:22,698
Yes. Which is why...

942
00:58:24,700 --> 00:58:27,160
Hm? Wait, me too?

943
00:58:27,244 --> 00:58:29,746
(Coronal) Yes
(Wistario) Cature, hurry up!

944
00:58:34,167 --> 00:58:36,128
We'll win the Urdr-Hunt...

945
00:58:36,211 --> 00:58:38,338
And make our dreams come true!

946
00:58:38,422 --> 00:58:39,756
Yeah

947
00:58:41,967 --> 00:58:43,176
Definitely!

948
00:58:46,013 --> 00:58:48,056
(N) Nadezhda

949
00:58:48,140 --> 00:58:51,977
Have you determined
the location of the final key?

950
00:58:52,060 --> 00:58:54,229
(Nadezhda) Yes, my lord

951
00:58:54,312 --> 00:58:57,107
However, what was revealed
was not coordinates...

952
00:58:57,899 --> 00:58:59,860
But a unique frequency

953
00:59:00,777 --> 00:59:02,612
(N) Just as I thought

954
00:59:02,696 --> 00:59:04,114
Either way...

955
00:59:04,781 --> 00:59:07,993
This will finally bring
the Urdr-Hunt to an end

956
00:59:12,581 --> 00:59:15,417
(Cyclase) So... the time has come...

957
00:59:19,212 --> 00:59:21,214
♪～

958
01:01:07,279 --> 01:01:09,281
～♪

959
01:01:11,366 --> 01:01:13,368
♪～

960
01:03:22,038 --> 01:03:24,040
～♪

960.2
01:03:34,250 --> 01:03:38,750
Mobile Suit Gundam: Iron-Blooded Orphans
10th Anniversary

960.4
01:03:38,750 --> 01:03:41,700
Wedge of Interposition

961
01:03:51,151 --> 01:03:54,529
(Mikazuki) Phew...

962
01:03:56,740 --> 01:04:01,161
(Ahab Reactor whirring)

963
01:04:18,762 --> 01:04:19,804
(Shino) Mmm...

964
01:04:20,805 --> 01:04:21,806
(Sniffing)

965
01:04:21,890 --> 01:04:26,102
(Shino) When Barbatos fights,
it smells like money

966
01:04:26,186 --> 01:04:29,856
(Eugene) Tekkadan's gonna get
even bigger now

967
01:04:33,985 --> 01:04:36,571
(Akihiro) Tch, I still think I should've...


969
01:04:36,655 --> 01:04:38,073
(Yukinojo) Don't be stupid.

970
01:04:38,740 --> 01:04:41,493
(Yukinojo) It's because you and Gusion
are standing by...

971
01:04:41,576 --> 01:04:43,578
that Mikazuki can fight so recklessly.

972
01:04:44,829 --> 01:04:45,830
Besides...

973
01:04:45,914 --> 01:04:48,166
(Ride) Whoa...
(Yukinojo) It's already over.

974
01:04:48,249 --> 01:04:49,709
Huh?

975
01:04:49,793 --> 01:04:50,627
Ah!

976
01:04:50,710 --> 01:04:56,132
(Battle sounds)

977
01:04:56,216 --> 01:04:57,258
(Boss) Tch...

978
01:05:02,972 --> 01:05:04,349
(Pilot A)
Damn it, quit darting around!

979
01:05:04,432 --> 01:05:06,643
Hey! Can someone
get behind him?

980
01:05:06,726 --> 01:05:07,769
Ah!

981
01:05:14,484 --> 01:05:16,236
(Pilot A) Stop moving...
(Pilot B) In front! In front!

982
01:05:16,319 --> 01:05:17,153
Ah! Ugh!

983
01:05:19,030 --> 01:05:21,574
(Orga) Finish 'em, Mika!

984
01:05:28,998 --> 01:05:32,419
Ah! Ngh...

985
01:05:55,734 --> 01:05:57,193
(Ride) Alright!
(Shino) Alright!

986
01:05:57,277 --> 01:05:58,194
(Akihiro) Naturally.

987
01:06:01,406 --> 01:06:02,449
(Orga) Well then...

988
01:06:02,991 --> 01:06:07,328
Just as requested,
a two-on-one handicap match.

989
01:06:08,246 --> 01:06:10,206
No complaints now, right?

990
01:06:10,290 --> 01:06:11,833
(Boss) I get it.

991
01:06:11,916 --> 01:06:13,084
Hey!

992
01:06:14,252 --> 01:06:16,087
(Yamagi) Make sure everything's secured!

993
01:06:16,171 --> 01:06:18,548
We'll handle the rest
once we're back!

994
01:06:18,631 --> 01:06:21,551
Tie down the smaller stuff
with belts together!

995
01:06:21,634 --> 01:06:23,928
If we don't hurry,
it'll be morning already!

996
01:06:24,012 --> 01:06:25,096
(Gunshot)

997
01:06:26,556 --> 01:06:27,849
(Pilot A) Gah! Help...

998
01:06:27,932 --> 01:06:29,350
(Gunshot)

999
01:06:30,310 --> 01:06:31,853
(Ride) That's brutal...

1000
01:06:31,936 --> 01:06:35,565
Just because they lost,
they didn't have to kill them.

1001
01:06:35,648 --> 01:06:37,901
(Shino) Those guys
were pretty well-known...

1002
01:06:37,984 --> 01:06:40,945
in mobile suit combat circles,
weren't they?

1003
01:06:41,029 --> 01:06:44,240
(Akihiro) Yeah, but they were
Human Debris.

1004
01:06:44,908 --> 01:06:46,743
That's what happens when they lose.

1005
01:06:48,411 --> 01:06:50,246
What a rotten world.

1006
01:06:51,164 --> 01:06:54,375
Though we're not exactly
much better ourselves.

1007
01:06:54,459 --> 01:06:56,002
(Mikazuki) I can still fight.

1008
01:06:56,085 --> 01:06:59,964
Maybe you can,
but Barbatos is screaming in pain.

1009
01:07:00,048 --> 01:07:02,926
Yamagi! Contact Teiwaz!

1010
01:07:03,009 --> 01:07:04,886
Make arrangements to send
this thing to the Saisei...

1011
01:07:04,969 --> 01:07:06,304
Not yet!

1012
01:07:08,431 --> 01:07:09,516
Not yet.

1013
01:07:09,599 --> 01:07:11,976
(Yamagi)
You don't want me to contact them?

1014
01:07:12,060 --> 01:07:13,520
(Yukinojo) Hah...

1015
01:07:13,603 --> 01:07:16,147
Yeah, leave it be!

1016
01:07:16,981 --> 01:07:18,024
That guy...

1017
01:07:18,107 --> 01:07:22,445
(Yukinojo)
Can't be helped.
Guess we'll just have them send more weapons again.

1018
01:07:22,529 --> 01:07:26,115
(Mikazuki)
Tell them to send something better this time.

1019
01:07:26,491 --> 01:07:28,993
(Yukinojo)
Teiwaz got a kick out of...

1020
01:07:29,077 --> 01:07:31,538
the combat data from that katana of yours.

1021
01:07:31,621 --> 01:07:34,415
That's why they only send those now.

1022
01:07:34,499 --> 01:07:37,418
Besides, with Barbatos in its current state...

1023
01:07:37,502 --> 01:07:42,048
if you tried swinging around a huge mace,
it'd fall apart.

1024
01:07:42,131 --> 01:07:43,341
(Mikazuki) Mm...

1025
01:07:43,675 --> 01:07:46,344
(President)
Then please sign here.

1026
01:07:48,263 --> 01:07:49,097
(Orga) Mm...

1027
01:07:59,190 --> 01:08:00,233
Will this do?

1028
01:08:01,901 --> 01:08:03,820
(Employee)
Yes, no problems here.

1029
01:08:03,903 --> 01:08:04,737
(Orga) Good.

1030
01:08:05,321 --> 01:08:07,532
Then the deal's settled.

1031
01:08:07,615 --> 01:08:12,078
Your miners will be working
under our umbrella from now on.

1032
01:08:12,579 --> 01:08:14,414
(President)
Tekkadan...

1033
01:08:14,497 --> 01:08:17,083
It's great that business is going well, but...

1034
01:08:17,166 --> 01:08:22,839
you shouldn't think
this kind of business will last forever.

1035
01:08:27,802 --> 01:08:30,179
(Eugene)
Like we need him to tell us that.

1036
01:08:30,263 --> 01:08:31,806
Now, now...

1037
01:08:31,890 --> 01:08:35,059
Let the losers bark all they want.

1038
01:08:35,143 --> 01:08:35,977
Right?

1039
01:08:36,060 --> 01:08:37,478
(Orga) Hm?

1040
01:08:38,146 --> 01:08:39,063
Mm...

1041
01:08:39,147 --> 01:08:40,106
(Atra) Mikazuki!
(Orga) Ah!

1042
01:08:40,189 --> 01:08:42,150
(Atra) Want another helping?
(Orga) Ah, sorry. What is it?

1043
01:08:42,233 --> 01:08:43,651
(Mikazuki) Yeah.
(Shino) Ah...

1044
01:08:43,735 --> 01:08:46,112
(Shino)
Looks like you're pretty busy.

1045
01:08:46,195 --> 01:08:49,782
(Orga)
Ah, yeah.
I've got some homework from the young lady...

1046
01:08:49,866 --> 01:08:50,742
Ah!

1047
01:08:50,825 --> 01:08:53,161
Crap! I'm already late for...

1048
01:08:53,244 --> 01:08:54,996
(Atra) Ah, your food!
(Orga) I'll eat later!

1049
01:08:55,079 --> 01:08:56,372
(Ride) Hey, Boss!

1050
01:08:56,456 --> 01:08:57,540
What?!

1051
01:08:58,041 --> 01:09:01,002
(Ride)
Um... there's a hole in your pants.

1052
01:09:01,085 --> 01:09:02,879
(Akihiro) In the butt.
(Orga) Ah!

1053
01:09:02,962 --> 01:09:05,632
(Atra)
Ah, I can sew it up right away.
Just leave it out for me...

1054
01:09:05,715 --> 01:09:06,549
(Orga) No!

1055
01:09:06,633 --> 01:09:09,052
It's fine. I'm in a hurry.

1056
01:09:11,679 --> 01:09:12,847
(Eugene)
Seriously...

1057
01:09:12,931 --> 01:09:15,558
Orga already knows that
without being told.

1058
01:09:15,642 --> 01:09:17,477
(Shino)
Yeah, about the hole in his ass?

1059
01:09:17,560 --> 01:09:19,312
(Eugene)
The business, idiot! The business!

1060
01:09:19,395 --> 01:09:22,482
(Shino)
That it can't keep going like this forever?

1061
01:09:22,565 --> 01:09:25,735
(Akihiro)
Orga's working hard
to make sure it does last.

1062
01:09:25,818 --> 01:09:29,280
(Shino)
Yeah, hard enough
not to notice the hole in his ass.

1063
01:09:29,364 --> 01:09:30,823
(Eugene)
I know that already.

1064
01:09:33,076 --> 01:09:35,078
He's our representative...

1065
01:09:35,161 --> 01:09:38,581
doing his best
with this unfamiliar business stuff.

1066
01:09:39,624 --> 01:09:43,086
(Ride)
Yeah, but if our representative's
walking around with a hole like that...

1067
01:09:43,169 --> 01:09:44,796
that's not very cool.

1068
01:09:44,879 --> 01:09:48,091
Ah! I know!
I've got a great idea!

1069
01:09:48,174 --> 01:09:49,801
(Mikazuki)
A great idea?

1070
01:09:51,386 --> 01:09:52,971
(Kudelia)
I'm impressed.

1071
01:09:53,513 --> 01:09:56,182
(Kudelia)
There are still some issues here and there, but...

1072
01:09:56,265 --> 01:09:57,100
Mm-hm.

1073
01:09:57,684 --> 01:09:59,811
You seem to understand it now.

1074
01:09:59,894 --> 01:10:02,939
So you really did read
the materials I gave you.

1075
01:10:03,022 --> 01:10:04,607
(Orga)
Hmph.
You're the one...

1076
01:10:04,691 --> 01:10:06,567
who told me to read them, young lady.

1077
01:10:06,651 --> 01:10:08,361
(Kudelia)
And besides...
(Orga) Hey!

1078
01:10:09,278 --> 01:10:11,823
(Kudelia)
You've improved quite a bit.

1079
01:10:13,199 --> 01:10:15,493
You were the one who told me...

1080
01:10:15,576 --> 01:10:17,495
people would look down on me
if I didn't have a proper signature.

1081
01:10:18,037 --> 01:10:22,875
Seriously, why do official contracts
need handwritten signatures anyway?

1082
01:10:22,959 --> 01:10:25,920
I'd never even held a pen before.

1083
01:10:26,003 --> 01:10:29,382
But now you can write
such a wonderful signature.

1084
01:10:29,465 --> 01:10:32,010
(Orga) Mm... Mmm...

1085
01:10:32,593 --> 01:10:34,721
(Kudelia)
As expected of the Commander.

1086
01:10:34,804 --> 01:10:37,348
Ah, come to think of it,
it's getting pretty late.

1087
01:10:37,432 --> 01:10:39,142
(Orga)
Maybe we should grab a bite...
(Knock)

1088
01:10:39,225 --> 01:10:40,685
Yeah, come in.

1089
01:10:41,644 --> 01:10:43,563
(Yamagi)
Um, Commander...

1090
01:10:43,646 --> 01:10:47,483
Everyone said to come to the
cafeteria once you're done here.

1091
01:10:47,942 --> 01:10:49,152
(Both)
Hm?

1092
01:10:54,782 --> 01:10:57,160
(Orga)
Ah... Ah...

1093
01:10:57,243 --> 01:10:59,328
F... For me?

1094
01:10:59,412 --> 01:11:01,122
It's a present from all of us.

1095
01:11:01,205 --> 01:11:03,207
(Akihiro)
"All of us?"
(Shino) Uh...

1096
01:11:03,291 --> 01:11:05,960
(Shino)
C'mon, don't sweat the details.

1097
01:11:06,043 --> 01:11:08,546
(Kudelia)
My! What a wonderful suit!

1098
01:11:08,629 --> 01:11:11,090
You should try it on, Commander!

1099
01:11:11,174 --> 01:11:12,008
Wow...

1100
01:11:12,091 --> 01:11:14,260
O... Okay...

1101
01:11:14,343 --> 01:11:16,345
(Clothes rustling)

1102
01:11:22,435 --> 01:11:26,105
(All)
Ooooh!

1103
01:11:26,189 --> 01:11:27,356
(Atra)
You look awesome!

1104
01:11:27,440 --> 01:11:28,733
(Kudelia)
It suits you perfectly!

1105
01:11:28,816 --> 01:11:30,610
(Yamagi)
You look smart.

1106
01:11:30,693 --> 01:11:33,738
(Eugene)
Yeah, seriously.
Fits you perfectly too.

1107
01:11:33,821 --> 01:11:35,490
(Mikazuki)
Mm-hm, mm-hm.

1108
01:11:35,573 --> 01:11:38,201
(Ride)
You look super strong or something!

1109
01:11:38,284 --> 01:11:39,368
(Shino)
Seriously!

1110
01:11:39,452 --> 01:11:41,370
(Orga)
This feels really weird.

1111
01:11:42,872 --> 01:11:45,374
But... thanks.

1112
01:11:45,458 --> 01:11:47,877
(All)
Heh... Hahahaha...

1113
01:11:47,960 --> 01:11:50,505
(Eugene)
Hey, Orga,
turn around for us.

1114
01:11:50,588 --> 01:11:52,089
(Orga)
Huh? L... Like this?

1115
01:11:52,173 --> 01:11:54,467
(Shino)
Bwahahaha!
Looking good, Orga!

1116
01:11:54,550 --> 01:11:56,928
(Ride)
So cool, Commander!

1117
01:11:57,011 --> 01:12:00,890
(All) Hahahahaha...
(Ride) Woo!

1118
01:12:02,225 --> 01:12:03,059
(Atra)
Hey...

1119
01:12:03,142 --> 01:12:05,561
Is this how you're supposed
to tie a necktie?

1120
01:12:05,645 --> 01:12:08,147
It does feel like
something's off...

1121
01:12:08,231 --> 01:12:09,816
Ah... wasn't it like this?

1122
01:12:09,899 --> 01:12:11,150
(Orga) Ghk!
(Yamagi) Hey, Shino, idiot...

1123
01:12:11,234 --> 01:12:12,068
What are you doing?!

1124
01:12:12,151 --> 01:12:13,319
(Orga)
Hey! Ghk...

1125
01:12:13,402 --> 01:12:16,823
(Eugene)
Man, that looks awful.
Let me see it.

1126
01:12:16,906 --> 01:12:18,324
It suits him.

1127
01:12:18,407 --> 01:12:21,828
Yeah. That's Orga's new weapon.

1128
01:12:22,912 --> 01:12:24,789
Maybe you need one too.

1129
01:12:24,872 --> 01:12:25,706
(Mikazuki)
Hm?

1130
01:12:26,666 --> 01:12:28,501
(Akihiro)
You should rely on us sometimes.

1131
01:12:29,585 --> 01:12:32,713
Or what?
Are we that unreliable?

1132
01:12:34,382 --> 01:12:35,591
Not sure.

1133
01:12:35,675 --> 01:12:37,552
Hey... you...

1134
01:12:37,635 --> 01:12:38,761
(Ride)
Hey, Boss...

1135
01:12:38,845 --> 01:12:41,848
If you're wearing that,
you don't need this anymore, right?

1136
01:12:42,431 --> 01:12:44,058
Give it to me!

1137
01:12:44,141 --> 01:12:47,353
(Orga) You're still too young for that.
(Ride) Heh... eheh...

1138
01:12:47,436 --> 01:12:50,898
Maybe when you get a little bigger.

1139
01:12:50,982 --> 01:12:53,317
(Ride) You really mean it?
(Orga) Yeah, I do.

1140
01:12:53,401 --> 01:12:57,446
(Orga)
The only one I can trust
with my back on the battlefield is Akihiro.

1141
01:12:57,530 --> 01:12:58,614
(Akihiro)
Hmph...

1142
01:13:05,580 --> 01:13:08,624
(Footsteps)

1143
01:13:08,708 --> 01:13:09,876
(Orga)
So...

1144
01:13:09,959 --> 01:13:12,587
So you're finally taking
it to the Saisei, huh?

1145
01:13:13,296 --> 01:13:15,464
(Mikazuki)
Akihiro said he'd handle it.

1146
01:13:16,173 --> 01:13:17,383
(Orga)
I see.

1147
01:13:18,176 --> 01:13:20,887
Well, I've got a new weapon too.

1148
01:13:22,346 --> 01:13:23,848
We'll be fine.

1149
01:13:23,931 --> 01:13:26,017
(Mikazuki)
Yeah... and...

1151
01:13:26,100 --> 01:13:31,022
I've got a few things I want to
say directly to the Teiwaz guys over there.

1152
01:13:31,522 --> 01:13:33,524
(Orga)
Got a complaint or something?

1153
01:13:35,526 --> 01:13:38,738
I'm sick of that pain in
the ass katana thing.

1154
01:13:38,821 --> 01:13:42,617
It looks cool when you use it, though.

1155
01:13:42,700 --> 01:13:45,328
But it's useless in group battles...

1156
01:13:45,786 --> 01:13:50,833
and more than anything,
it's not enough to clear your path, Orga.

1157
01:13:52,084 --> 01:13:54,337
Heh... I see.

1158
01:13:56,047 --> 01:13:59,091
(Mikazuki)
To see the place you're aiming for...

1159
01:14:00,760 --> 01:14:05,056
I have to keep giving everything I've got.

1160
01:14:05,514 --> 01:14:06,349
(Orga)
Yeah.

1161
01:14:07,350 --> 01:14:08,601
I'll show you...

1162
01:14:09,477 --> 01:14:13,230
All kinds of great things.
For all of you.

1163
01:14:13,314 --> 01:14:14,231
(Mikazuki)
Yeah.

1164
01:14:14,315 --> 01:14:16,317
♪～

1165
01:14:19,862 --> 01:14:21,864
♪ Raise your flag

1166
01:14:21,948 --> 01:14:23,532
♪ With all your voice

1167
01:14:23,616 --> 01:14:25,201
♪ With all your voice

1168
01:14:25,284 --> 01:14:28,454
♪ Shout it out loud with all your voice

1169
01:14:28,537 --> 01:14:30,164
♪ One day

1170
01:14:30,248 --> 01:14:31,832
♪ Someday somewhere

1171
01:14:31,916 --> 01:14:37,588
♪ Dream on as we wander

1172
01:14:37,672 --> 01:14:40,967
♪ Under pressure
You are waiting for directions

1173
01:14:41,050 --> 01:14:44,220
♪ Going on the road
Without your mind

1174
01:14:44,303 --> 01:14:47,556
♪ All misleads they give
Ignoring our decisions

1175
01:14:47,640 --> 01:14:50,851
♪ Killing yourself your soul
we have inside

1176
01:14:50,935 --> 01:14:54,146
♪ Continue the struggle
and feel like you're discouraged

1177
01:14:54,230 --> 01:14:57,441
♪ Rise up again to run to the end

1178
01:14:57,525 --> 01:14:59,193
♪ In between

1179
01:14:59,276 --> 01:15:00,778
♪ The never ending dream

1180
01:15:00,861 --> 01:15:06,284
♪ We can struggle and muzzle
the world before it fades away

1181
01:15:06,367 --> 01:15:08,285
♪ Raise your flag

1182
01:15:08,369 --> 01:15:09,912
♪ With all your voice

1183
01:15:09,996 --> 01:15:11,539
♪ With all your voice

1184
01:15:11,622 --> 01:15:14,834
♪ Shout it out loud with all your voice

1185
01:15:14,917 --> 01:15:16,502
♪ One day

1186
01:15:16,585 --> 01:15:18,170
♪ Someday somewhere

1187
01:15:18,254 --> 01:15:21,382
♪ Believing that we will reach that goal

1188
01:15:21,465 --> 01:15:23,009
♪ Come on and raise your flag

1189
01:15:23,092 --> 01:15:24,760
♪ So just raise your flag

1190
01:15:24,844 --> 01:15:28,097
♪ No matter how many times
we feel defeated or lost

1191
01:15:28,180 --> 01:15:29,682
♪ As long as we breathe

1192
01:15:29,765 --> 01:15:31,392
♪ As long as we carry on

1193
01:15:31,475 --> 01:15:37,481
♪ Dream on as we wander

1194
01:15:41,152 --> 01:15:43,154
~♪

1195
01:15:44,613 --> 01:15:46,615
♪～

1196
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:53,000
Translation, Editing, Re-Timing
Drakanwolf

1197
01:15:55,000 --> 01:15:58,000
QA Check
TeknoMonkey

1198
